2026-09-27T04:47:58.5288409Z Update Note
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5288621Z ===========
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5288924Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5289226Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5289331Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5289553Z ================
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5289703Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5289854Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5290258Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5290489Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5290601Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5290907Z ====================================
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5291093Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5291247Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5291663Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5292039Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5371690Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5372370Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5372535Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5373121Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5373679Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5374003Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5374355Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5374882Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5374973Z Packages
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5375174Z ========
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5375296Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5376613Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5377981Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5378218Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5378699Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5379171Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5379748Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5380303Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5380739Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5381008Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5381553Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5381821Z ==========================
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5381965Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5383073Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5384489Z 
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5385254Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5386134Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T04:47:58.5386364Z 
